From: Christopher Stenger
Subject: h713: V2 A/B boot through Standard Boot's RAUC method

The projector (HY200_QZ713_V2) boots A/B with U-Boot's own bootmeth_rauc
(no board code): slot A is boot_a (p5) + root_a (p9), slot B is boot_b (p6) +
root_b (p16). bootmeth_rauc takes an attempt from the first slot in
BOOT_ORDER with BOOT_<slot>_LEFT left, saves the environment, and runs the
boot.scr on that slot's vfat boot partition with rauc.slot=<slot>; when no
slot has attempts left it refills them all and resets. RAUC in Linux marks
the booted slot good and drives updates.

Everything is declared, nothing is scripted: the V2 -u-boot.dtsi gives
the bootstd node bootdev-order = "mmc1" and a single rauc bootmeth node, so
only that method is bound, and the boot command is Standard Boot's default
"bootflow scan -lb". V2 drops the deprecated DISTRO_DEFAULTS, and
sunxi-common.h now includes the distro_bootcmd environment only for boards
that keep it: its boot_targets list (fel mmc_auto usb0 pxe dhcp) would
otherwise override the devicetree order and names nothing bootable here.
The bench (A1) keeps DISTRO_DEFAULTS and its environment is unchanged.
V2's PREBOOT also drops "usb start": U-Boot has no USB host on this board
(only the fastboot/UMS gadget), and CMD_USB went with DISTRO_DEFAULTS.

The environment is now written on every boot, so it becomes redundant: a
second 64 KiB copy at 0x93d90000, right after the first, still inside the
GPT partition "empty".

diff -ruN a/arch/arm/dts/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713-v2-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713-v2-u-boot.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm/dts/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713-v2-u-boot.dtsi	2026-11-20 09:20:09.893905495 -0800
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713-v2-u-boot.dtsi	2026-11-20 09:20:24.511681718 -0800
@@ -1,3 +1,19 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0+
 
 #include "sun50i-h713-u-boot.dtsi"
+
+/ {
+	/*
+	 * Standard Boot: boot only from the eMMC (mmc1) and only through the
+	 * RAUC A/B method. Declaring a bootmeth here binds just that one,
+	 * instead of every bootmeth U-Boot was built with.
+	 */
+	bootstd {
+		compatible = "u-boot,boot-std";
+		bootdev-order = "mmc1";
+
+		rauc {
+			compatible = "u-boot,distro-rauc";
+		};
+	};
+};
diff -ruN a/configs/hy200_qz713_v2_defconfig b/configs/hy200_qz713_v2_defconfig
--- a/configs/hy200_qz713_v2_defconfig	2026-11-20 09:20:09.897148762 -0800
+++ b/configs/hy200_qz713_v2_defconfig	2026-11-20 09:21:12.584956762 -0800
@@ -31,4 +31,27 @@
 CONFIG_SUNXI_DRAM_H713_LPDDR3_STOCK=y
 # No H713_MIPS_BOOT and no h713_disp in PREBOOT yet: the display path is
 # untested here and panel power differs (PH19). Phase 4 step 2 adds them.
-CONFIG_PREBOOT="if itest.l *0x0709011c == 0xfa57b007; then mw.l 0x0709011c 0; run fastboot_mode; elif itest.l *0x0709011c == 0xb007c0de; then mw.l 0x0709011c 0; setenv bootdelay -1; fi; usb start"
+# No "usb start" either: U-Boot has no USB host on this board ("No USB
+# controllers found"), only the gadget for fastboot/UMS, and CMD_USB goes
+# with DISTRO_DEFAULTS.
+CONFIG_PREBOOT="if itest.l *0x0709011c == 0xfa57b007; then mw.l 0x0709011c 0; run fastboot_mode; elif itest.l *0x0709011c == 0xb007c0de; then mw.l 0x0709011c 0; setenv bootdelay -1; fi"
+# A/B boot with Standard Boot's RAUC method (boot/bootmeth_rauc.c): slot A is
+# boot_a (p5) + root_a (p9), slot B is boot_b (p6) + root_b (p16). It takes
+# an attempt from the first slot in BOOT_ORDER with BOOT_<slot>_LEFT > 0, saves
+# the environment, and runs boot.scr from that slot's boot partition (vfat)
+# with rauc.slot=<slot> in raucargs; Linux's RAUC marks the slot good. The
+# boot device (mmc1) and the only boot method (rauc) are declared in the
+# bootstd node of sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713-v2-u-boot.dtsi, so the boot command
+# is Standard Boot's default, "bootflow scan -lb". No DISTRO_DEFAULTS: its
+# distro_bootcmd environment (boot_targets) would override that order.
+# The environment is saved on every boot, so keep two copies (both in the GPT
+# partition "empty").
+# CONFIG_DISTRO_DEFAULTS is not set
+CONFIG_BOOTSTD_FULL=y
+CONFIG_ENV_REDUNDANT=y
+CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET_REDUND=0x93d90000
+CONFIG_BOOTMETH_RAUC=y
+CONFIG_BOOTMETH_RAUC_BOOT_ORDER="A B"
+CONFIG_BOOTMETH_RAUC_PARTITIONS="5,9 6,16"
+CONFIG_BOOTMETH_RAUC_DEFAULT_TRIES=3
+CONFIG_BOOTMETH_RAUC_RESET_ALL_ZERO_TRIES=y
diff -ruN a/include/configs/sunxi-common.h b/include/configs/sunxi-common.h
--- a/include/configs/sunxi-common.h	2026-11-20 09:20:09.893127974 -0800
+++ b/include/configs/sunxi-common.h	2026-11-20 09:20:24.520279196 -0800
@@ -242,7 +242,17 @@
 #define BOOTCMD_SUNXI_COMPAT
 #endif
 
+/*
+ * The distro_bootcmd environment (boot_targets, distro_bootcmd, the scan
+ * scripts) only for boards that still use it. A Standard Boot board leaves
+ * DISTRO_DEFAULTS off, and a boot_targets list here would override the boot
+ * device order its devicetree declares.
+ */
+#ifdef CONFIG_DISTRO_DEFAULTS
 #include <config_distro_bootcmd.h>
+#else
+#define BOOTENV
+#endif
 
